<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uraniborg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1576">1576</a>–<a href="/years/1580">1580</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uraniborg was the observatory and residence built by the astronomer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tycho-brahe">Tycho Brahe</a> on the island of Ven in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oresund">Øresund</a>, with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-denmark">Frederick II of Denmark</a>, from 1576. Designed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> palace with instruments, a library, workshops and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press, it was supplemented by the underground observatory of Stjerneborg. It was abandoned after Tycho left in 1597 and later demolished.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uraniborg.jpg" alt="Uraniborg" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stanlekub · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uraniborgskiss_45.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
